Original commit body from 15257c7c108f79a16cf8734e40493919fd89d72e:

_manifest_selected_tests ends both of its branches in a grep chain, and a grep
that matches nothing exits 1. On a manifest that selects NO tests -- what
smart-test correctly writes for any docs-only or config-only diff -- sed emits
only the marker line, the first grep drops it and exits 1, and the second gets
no input and exits 1 too. Every caller runs under set -euo pipefail
(scripts/auto-pr:3), so that status killed the shell before the function's own
`return 0` could mask it.

The failure was total rather than partial: exit 1 at "Regenerating test
manifest...", no PR, no .git/PR_PENDING gate, no branch on the remote, and a
log that simply stops.

WHERE IT CAME FROM. _manifest_union landed one day earlier (INV-bigaz) to stop
the regen DROPPING an author's hand-widened manifest, and it calls
_manifest_selected_tests twice inside a pipeline group. It destroyed the entire
run instead of narrowing it, in exactly the population it was written to
defend. It went unseen because the last docs-only manifest committed before the
guard predates it, so nothing had exercised the empty case.

`|| true` on BOTH branches makes "this manifest selects nothing" the
empty-output success it always meant to be. Both, because the marker-less
branch serves manifests written before the sections existed, and half a fix is
how a defect survives its own patch.

THE TESTS NOW RUN UNDER THE CALLER'S SHELL OPTIONS, which is why this was
catchable at all. tests/test_autopr_manifest_union.py sourced the library into
a plain `bash -c` with errexit and pipefail OFF, so the non-zero status was
discarded and thirteen tests passed over a function that could not survive its
own caller. The harness now sets the options before the source, exactly as
auto-pr does. All thirteen still pass; seven new cases pin the empty selection
end to end.

SECOND DEFECT, SAME FUNCTION: THE HEADER CONTRADICTED THE BODY. The union
copies the header verbatim from the regen -- which is what preserves "# Mode:"
and the CHANGED_SOURCE_FILES section CI parses separately -- and thereby copied
the regen's own "# Selected tests:" count, describing a body the union had just
replaced. After a docs-only union the file read "Selected tests: 0" over three
real paths. Nothing consumes that count today (ci.yml:935 recomputes it from
the body it is about to run; the pre-commit hook gates only on
"# Mode: full-suite"), so this was a manifest that lied rather than one that
broke. It is fixed anyway: "CI runs nothing while reporting success" is the
precise failure _manifest_union's own FAIL-SAFE comment says it exists to
prevent, and a header already reading 0 is that failure pre-staged for
whichever consumer trusts it first. The count is restated from what was
actually written, after the existence filter, and only ever as a correction --
a header carrying no count line does not gain one.

LIVE EVIDENCE, real committed manifest (334 paths) against a real
zero-selection regen, both arms under set -euo pipefail:
  pre-fix library:  exit 1, no output file written at all
  post-fix library: exit 0, all 334 paths preserved, header restated 0 -> 334

Tests: 1657 passed across 96 affected files; mypy strict ratchet clean at 669.

